Pixelado layer on BananaDS (SuperDrastic bananads/), part 1 of 2.

Local multiplayer over the network the console is on (LAN), the Party session (one emulator
process the app keeps, wifi.lobbyctl_dir), booting the DS firmware for DS Download Play,
the DS's MAC from /etc/machine-id in the generated and the user's firmware, the saved
Nintendo WFC settings, Auto and Auto Join, the in-game menu's Local multiplayer row,
and the Spanish lines for them until BananaOS's language pack has them.
Also commits the three patches BananaOS applies to BananaDS at build time (the help line
above the Back button, the remappable pad buttons, the left stick's 45-degree octants).

